-- EU AI Act, Article 73: a provider of a high-risk AI system reports a
-- serious incident. With Article 75(1) and (1a) as inserted by Regulation (EU)
-- 2026/1744 (who receives the report), Article 2(2) (Section B products),
-- Article 20(2) (the duty to inform of a risk) and Article 26(5) (the
-- deployer's part).
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Days are calendar days: Article 73 says "days" and nothing more. The day
-- the provider becomes aware is day 0, so "not later than 15 days after"
-- makes day 15 the last day. Regulation (EEC, Euratom) No 1182/71 on periods
-- and time limits may bear on this and is not deposited: FORK F7.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-domain`
IMPORT `aia-dates`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`

§ `Article 73: reporting of serious incidents`

§§ `Article 2(2): products under Section B of Annex I`

-- src:420 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply.
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:136 | ‘2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply.
-- Neither version lets Article 73 reach a Section B product.
@ref Article 2(2) (src:420); as replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(2)(a) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:136)
GIVEN s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2(2) leaves my system outside Article 73` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Article 6(1), product under Section B of Annex I` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article 73(1): who must report`

-- src:1730 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems placed on the Union market shall report any serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where that incident occurred.
@ref Article 73(1) (src:1730); Article 113 and Article 111(2) in aia-dates.l4
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 73 applies to my system on` `the date` v s MEANS
        `I am the provider of the AI system` s
    AND s's `the system has been placed on the Union market`
    AND (NOT (`Article 2(2) leaves my system outside Article 73` s))
    AND `Article 73 is in application for my system on` `the date` v s
    AND `Article 111(2) lets the Regulation reach my system on` `the date` v s

@ref Article 113, as encoded in aia-dates.l4
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 73 is in application for my system on` `the date` v s MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date Article 73 applies from` v (s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST start THEN `the date` AT LEAST start

§§ `Article 73(9) and (10): reports limited to point (c) incidents`

-- src:1740 | 9. For high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that are placed on the market or put into service by providers that are subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those set out in this Regulation, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c).
@ref Article 73(9) (src:1740)
GIVEN s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 73(9) limits my reports to point (c) incidents` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Article 6(2), listed in Annex III` THEN s's `I am subject to Union instruments with equivalent incident-reporting obligations`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:1741 | 10. For high-risk AI systems which are safety components of devices, or are themselves devices, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c) of this Regulation, and shall be made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member States where the incident occurred.
@ref Article 73(10) (src:1741)
GIVEN s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 73(10) limits my reports to point (c) incidents` s MEANS
    s's `the system is or is a safety component of a device under Regulation 2017/745 or 2017/746`

§§ `Must I report?`

-- Article 73(1), narrowed by (9) and (10).
-- Article 75(1a) applies "Article 73 (2) to (9)" to the AI Office route, so
-- (9) narrows that route too, and (10) does NOT: a medical device that comes
-- under the AI Office (by Article 75(1)(b), since (a)(i) excludes Annex I
-- products) reports every serious incident, to the AI Office.
-- Whether Article 73 reaches the system is judged on the day the provider
-- became aware of the incident, not on the date the question is asked: the
-- duty arises with awareness, and every clock runs from that day. If the
-- Regulation did not reach the system on that day, no duty arose then, and a
-- later significant design change does not create one for that incident.
-- `the date` (asked) is kept as an input so every Article 73 question takes
-- the same facts; the seat derives the version in force from it. Open
-- question 7 in NOTES.md.
@ref Article 73(1), (9), (10) (src:1730) (src:1740-1741); Article 75(1a) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:434)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i MEANS
        `Article 73 applies to my system on` (i's `the date I became aware of it`) v s
    AND `the incident is a serious incident` i
    AND (    (     (NOT (`Article 73(9) limits my reports to point (c) incidents` s))
               AND (    (NOT (`Article 73(10) limits my reports to point (c) incidents` s))
                    OR  `the AI Office is exclusively competent for my system` v s))
         OR `point (c): infringement of fundamental-rights obligations` i)

§§ `To whom: Article 73(1), (10) and Article 75(1), (1a)`

-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:417 | ‘1. The AI Office shall be exclusively competent for the supervision and enforcement of the obligations under this Regulation in relation to the following AI systems:
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:418 | (a)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:419 | AI systems based on general-purpose AI models where the model and the system are developed by the same provider, or by providers forming part of the same undertaking as that provider, with the exception of:
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:420 | (i)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:421 | AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:422 | (ii)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:423 | AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III;
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:424 | (iii)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:425 | AI systems provided by law enforcement authorities, border management authorities and financial institutions, insofar as those AI systems fall under Article 74(6); and
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:426 | (iv)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:427 | AI systems referred to in point 8 of Annex III as regards the administration of justice;
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:428 | (b)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:429 | AI systems that constitute or that are integrated into a very large online platform or very large online search engine designated in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:430 | The exclusive competence referred to in the first subparagraph shall apply to the providers of those systems.
-- As enacted, Article 75(1) gave the AI Office no such competence over
-- systems, so this is FALSE for the enacted text.
@ref Article 75(1), as replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(31)(b) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:417-430)
GIVEN v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the AI Office is exclusively competent for my system` v s MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN
            (    s's `the system is based on a general-purpose AI model from me or my undertaking`
             AND (NOT (`the system is related to a product under Annex I` s))
             AND (NOT (s's `the system is listed in point 2 of Annex III`))
             AND (NOT (s's `the system is provided by an authority or financial institution within Article 74(6)`))
             AND (NOT (s's `the system is listed in point 8 of Annex III for the administration of justice`)))
        OR  s's `the system is or is part of a designated very large online platform or search engine`

@ref Article 75(1)(a)(i), as replaced (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:421)
GIVEN s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the system is related to a product under Annex I` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`
    WHEN `Article 6(1), product under Section A of Annex I` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Article 6(1), product under Section B of Annex I` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:434 | ‘1a. By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office. Article 73 (2) to (9), shall apply mutatis mutandis.
-- Verified: the deposited Omnibus does insert this paragraph (the arXiv
-- 2608.19278 claim). Article 73(10) is not among those applied; a device
-- under the medical-device Regulations is an Annex I product and so is
-- outside Article 75(1)(a) by exception (i) in any case.
@ref Article 75(1a), inserted by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(31)(c) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:434); Article 73(1) (src:1730); Article 73(10) (src:1741)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `recipient`
`to whom must I report under Article 73` `the date` v s i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    THEN BRANCH
            IF `the AI Office is exclusively competent for my system` v s
            THEN `the AI Office`
            IF `Article 73(10) limits my reports to point (c) incidents` s
            THEN `the national competent authority chosen by the Member State where the incident occurred`
            OTHERWISE `the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where the incident occurred`
    ELSE `no report is required of me`

§§ `By when: Article 73(2), (3) and (4)`

-- src:1731 | 2. The report referred to in paragraph 1 shall be made immediately after the provider has established a causal link between the AI system and the serious incident or the reasonable likelihood of such a link, and, in any event, not later than 15 days after the provider or, where applicable, the deployer, becomes aware of the serious incident.
-- src:1732 | The period for the reporting referred to in the first subparagraph shall take account of the severity of the serious incident.
-- src:1733 | 3. Notwithstanding paragraph 2 of this Article, in the event of a widespread infringement or a serious incident as defined in Article 3, point (49)(b), the report referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall be provided immediately, and not later than two days after the provider or, where applicable, the deployer becomes aware of that incident.
-- src:1734 | 4. Notwithstanding paragraph 2, in the event of the death of a person, the report shall be provided immediately after the provider or the deployer has established, or as soon as it suspects, a causal relationship between the high-risk AI system and the serious incident, but not later than 10 days after the date on which the provider or, where applicable, the deployer becomes aware of the serious incident.
-- The encoding computes the OUTER limit only. "Immediately" in each
-- paragraph, and "shall take account of the severity", are not numbers, and
-- may require an earlier report. Where (3) and (4) both apply (a death in a
-- widespread infringement), the earlier limit is taken: FORK F2.
@ref Article 73(2), (3), (4) (src:1731-1734)
GIVEN i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Article 73 outer limit in days` i MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the incident is a widespread infringement` i
            OR `point (b): disruption of critical infrastructure` i
        THEN 2
        IF i's `it led, directly or indirectly, to the death of a person`
        THEN 10
        OTHERWISE 15

-- The clock runs from the day the provider became aware. "Or, where
-- applicable, the deployer" is read as the case where the deployer reports
-- under Article 26(5): FORK F1.
@ref Article 73(2), (3), (4) (src:1731-1734)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must I report under Article 73` `the date` v s i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    THEN `no later than` (i's `the date I became aware of it` PLUS `the Article 73 outer limit in days` i)
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

@ref Article 73(2), (3), (4) (src:1731-1734)
GIVEN `the day of the report` IS A DATE, `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a report made on` `the day of the report` `is within the Article 73 outer limit for` `the date` v s i MEANS
    CONSIDER `by when must I report under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    WHEN `no later than` last THEN `the day of the report` AT MOST last
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article 73(5): an initial report that is incomplete`

-- src:1735 | 5. Where necessary to ensure timely reporting, the provider or, where applicable, the deployer, may submit an initial report that is incomplete, followed by a complete report.
-- Whether it is "necessary to ensure timely reporting" is the provider's
-- judgment, asked as a fact. No period is stated for the complete report.
@ref Article 73(5) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`, `necessary to ensure timely reporting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may I first submit an incomplete initial report` `the date` v s i `necessary to ensure timely reporting` MEANS
        `must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    AND `necessary to ensure timely reporting`

@ref Article 73(5) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must the complete report follow` `the date` v s i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    THEN `no period stated` "followed by a complete report"
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

§§ `Article 73(6): investigation after the report`

-- src:1736 | 6. Following the reporting of a serious incident pursuant to paragraph 1, the provider shall, without delay, perform the necessary investigations in relation to the serious incident and the AI system concerned. This shall include a risk assessment of the incident, and corrective action.
@ref Article 73(6), first subparagraph (src:1736)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must I investigate the incident` `the date` v s i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i
    THEN `no period stated` "without delay"
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

-- src:1737 | The provider shall cooperate with the competent authorities, and where relevant with the notified body concerned, during the investigations referred to in the first subparagraph, and shall not perform any investigation which involves altering the AI system concerned in a way which may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident, prior to informing the competent authorities of such action.
@ref Article 73(6), second subparagraph (src:1737)
GIVEN `the alteration may affect a later evaluation of the causes` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have informed the competent authorities of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may I alter the AI system in my investigation` `the alteration may affect a later evaluation of the causes` `I have informed the competent authorities of it` MEANS
        (NOT `the alteration may affect a later evaluation of the causes`)
    OR  `I have informed the competent authorities of it`

§§ `Article 73(8): what the authority must do with my report`

-- src:1739 | 8. The market surveillance authority shall take appropriate measures, as provided for in Article 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, within seven days from the date it received the notification referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, and shall follow the notification procedures as provided in that Regulation.
-- An official's duty, encoded for what it means to the provider: the date
-- by which measures are due. The receiving day is day 0.
@ref Article 73(8) (src:1739)
GIVEN `the date the authority received my report` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the authority to take measures on my report` `the date the authority received my report` MEANS
    `the date the authority received my report` PLUS 7

§§ `Article 20(2): informing of a risk`

-- src:951 | 2. Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1) and the provider becomes aware of that risk, it shall immediately investigate the causes, in collaboration with the reporting deployer, where applicable, and inform the market surveillance authorities competent for the high-risk AI system concerned and, where applicable, the notified body that issued a certificate for that high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 44, in particular, of the nature of the non-compliance and of any relevant corrective action taken.
-- Article 20 is in Chapter III, Section 3, so it takes the Chapter III date.
-- Whether the system "presents a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1)"
-- is asked as a fact; Article 79 is out of scope.
@ref Article 20(2) (src:951); Article 113 in aia-dates.l4
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I inform the market surveillance authorities under Article 20(2)` `the date` v s `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` MEANS
        `I am the provider of the AI system` s
    AND `Chapter III is in application for my system on` `the date` v s
    AND `Article 111(2) lets the Regulation reach my system on` `the date` v s
    AND `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it`

@ref Article 113, as encoded in aia-dates.l4
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter III is in application for my system on` `the date` v s MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply from` v (s's `the route by which the system is high-risk`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST start THEN `the date` AT LEAST start

@ref Article 20(2) (src:951)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must I inform under Article 20(2)` `the date` v s `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` MEANS
    IF `must I inform the market surveillance authorities under Article 20(2)` `the date` v s `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it`
    THEN `no period stated` "immediately"
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

-- Article 26(5), quoted and not encoded as a rule. It is the deployer's duty,
-- and the deployer has no seat here. It bears on the provider in two ways:
-- the deployer informs the provider first, which is one way the provider
-- "becomes aware"; and where the deployer cannot reach the provider, the
-- deployer reports under Article 73 itself, which is how this encoding reads
-- "or, where applicable, the deployer" in Article 73(2) to (5). FORK F1.
-- src:1023 | Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis.

§§ `End of Article 73`
